#: ../../../source/api/parameters/parameter_sets.rst:19
msgid "Adding Parameter Sets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/parameters/parameter_sets.rst:21
msgid ""
"Parameter sets can be added to PyBaMM by creating a python package, and "
"registering a `entry point`_ to ``pybamm_parameter_sets``. At a minimum, the "
"package (``cell_parameters``) should consist of the following::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/parameters/parameter_sets.rst:25
msgid ""
"cell_parameters\n"
"├── pyproject.toml        # and/or setup.cfg, setup.py\n"
"└── src\n"
"    └── cell_parameters\n"
"        └── cell_alpha.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/parameters/parameter_sets.rst:33
msgid ""
"The actual parameter set is defined within ``cell_alpha.py``, as shown "
"below. For an example, see the `Marquis2019`_ parameter sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/parameters/parameter_sets.rst:38
msgid ""
"import pybamm\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def get_parameter_values():\n"
"    \"\"\"Doc string for cell-alpha\"\"\"\n"
"    return {\n"
"        \"chemistry\": \"lithium_ion\",\n"
"        \"citation\": \"@book{van1995python, title={Python reference "
"manual}}\",\n"
"        # ...\n"
"    }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/parameters/parameter_sets.rst:52
msgid ""
"Then register ``get_parameter_values`` to ``pybamm_parameter_sets`` in "
"``pyproject.toml``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/parameters/parameter_sets.rst:54
msgid ""
"[project.entry-points.pybamm_parameter_sets]\n"
"cell_alpha = \"cell_parameters.cell_alpha:get_parameter_values\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/parameters/parameter_sets.rst:59
msgid ""
"If you are using ``setup.py`` or ``setup.cfg`` to setup your package, please "
"see SetupTools' documentation for registering `entry points`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/parameters/parameter_sets.rst:64
msgid ""
"If you're willing to open-source your parameter set, `let us know`_, and we "
"can add an entry to :ref:`third-party-parameter-sets`."
msgstr ""

